      "goal": "Implement the collapsible-group layer model: glyph-group.children[] controls per-sub-layer visibility and properties (hue, blend, opacity, visible), AND allows independent assets (e.g. a media layer) to be interleaved between named sub-layers. Title scene's CODECAINE acquires a children array placing an in-text media element between extrusion-shadow and chrome-top sub-layers, plus toggled visibility/hue on specific sub-layers.",
      "prerequisites": [2],
      "status": "pending",
      "testing_strategy": "Manual: title scene's logo shows the in-text media bleeding through the chrome layers correctly (visible behind chrome-top, in front of extrusion-shadow). Toggling a sub-layer's visible:false in scene.json hides only that named layer. Property edits (hue=180 on red-fill) visibly recolor only that sub-layer. Z-order within the group reflects array order in children.",
      "task_groups": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Visual Editor — Read-Only View (canvas, hierarchy, inspector, asset browser)",
      "goal": "Stand up the editor as a separate Vite entry. 4-panel layout: canvas preview (re-uses the renderer), hierarchy panel showing the collapsible layer tree with expand/collapse on glyph-groups, inspector panel showing the selected layer's properties read-only, and asset browser listing registry entries by type. Loads scenes/<id>/scene.json by URL param. Selecting a layer in the hierarchy highlights it on canvas and populates inspector.",
      "prerequisites": [3],
      "status": "pending",
      "testing_strategy": "Manual: open /editor?scene=title, see all 4 panels. Hierarchy tree matches scene.json layer order, glyph-groups collapse/expand. Selecting a sub-layer of CODECAINE shows its properties (visible, hue, blend) in inspector. Asset browser lists every registry entry grouped by type. No edits possible yet — read-only is the explicit floor.",
      "task_groups": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Editor Authoring — Drag, Edit, Reorder, Save",
      "goal": "Make the editor write-capable. Inspector inputs edit the in-memory scene and the canvas re-renders live. Drag from asset browser onto canvas adds a new layer at the drop position. Hierarchy supports drag-to-reorder and drag-into-group / drag-out-of-group. Save button persists the scene back to scenes/<id>/scene.json via a Vite middleware PUT endpoint. Loading picks up edits made externally (agent edits the same file on disk).",
      "prerequisites": [4],
      "status": "pending",
      "testing_strategy": "Manual: editor full authoring loop — drag the CODECAINE asset onto an empty scene, edit its position via inspector, reorder layers in hierarchy, save, reload page, confirm scene persists exactly. Edit scene.json on disk in another window, reload editor, confirm it reflects the external edit (proves agent-editability). Confirm save endpoint round-trips JSON without loss of properties or formatting differences that would break diffs.",
      "task_groups": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Component + Audio Asset Types, Title Scene Complete, Build/Export, Replace apps/frontend/",
      "goal": "Add the remaining two day-one asset types: component (data-driven JS — press-start with its blink animation) and audio (Web Audio playback). Title scene reaches full vertical-slice fidelity per spec success criteria: bg-video + CODECAINE (with children + interleaved media) + press-start + CRT + ambient audio cue. Multi-page Vite build emits one HTML page per scene, bundling all referenced assets, producing a deployable static site. Retire apps/frontend/.",
      "prerequisites": [5],
      "status": "pending",
      "testing_strategy": "Manual: title scene visually matches success-criteria checklist from spec.md (every item passes). press-start blinks. Audio plays/loops. Run vite build → dist/ contains one HTML per scene with bundled assets, no broken references. Serve dist/ statically (e.g. `npx serve dist/`) and confirm the title page renders identically to dev mode. apps/frontend/ deleted from working tree; no remaining import references from other apps.",
      "task_groups": []
    }
  ]
}

